course: dictionary
lesson: 15267
title: Sickly: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Sickly is an adjective, and what it means can change with the thing it describes. Use the clues around it, as you would with any new word. «The sickly baby needed a lot of rest.» The clue is needed a lot of rest, so sickly means often ill or weak.
explain: «The cake was sickly sweet, with three layers of icing.» Here sickly is not about being ill. The cake is so sweet that it makes you feel a bit sick. Ask yourself what is being described: a person, a taste, a colour or a feeling?
explain: «The walls were painted a sickly green.» A sickly colour is pale and unpleasant, not bright. Swap in pale and unpleasant. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Sickly means often ill, weak or not healthy.
fact: «Sickly» can also mean looking pale or unhealthy, as in «a sickly face».
fact: For taste or smell, «sickly sweet» means too sweet, so that it makes you feel a bit sick.
fact: For colour or light, «sickly» means pale and unpleasant, like «a sickly yellow».
fact: For feelings, «sickly» means too sweet or sentimental.
exercise: «The sickly child stayed in bed for a week.» What does sickly mean here? | Covered in sweets | *Often ill and weak | Very loud and cheerful | Brightly coloured
exercise: «The sauce was so sickly that Mia could only eat one spoonful.» What does sickly mean? | Cold and wet | Very old | Pale and pink | *Too sweet, so it makes you feel a bit sick
exercise: Which word in «The room was lit by a sickly light» tells you the light was pale and unpleasant? | light | *sickly | room | lit
test: «Her sickly smile told Dad she was not well.» What does sickly suggest? | Happy and bright | *Pale and unhealthy looking | Hungry for lunch | Angry at the rain
test: Sam says sickly always means ill. Is he right? | *No, it can also describe sweet tastes, pale colours and sentimental feelings | Yes, it only ever means ill | Yes, but only for animals | No, it means happy
exam: In «the sickly sweet perfume», what does sickly mean? | Pale and pretty | Very quiet | Often ill | *Too sweet, making you feel a bit sick
